VeridianOS: fixincludes, lto-plugin: const-correct strrchr results

GCC reported (the host compiler defaults to C23, where glibc's strrchr
returns const char * for a const char * argument):

  fixincludes/fixincl.c:747:22: warning: initialization discards 'const'
    qualifier from pointer target type [-Wdiscarded-qualifiers]
    (twice: fixincl is built for the build and for the host)
  lto-plugin/lto-plugin.c:1100:5 and 1152:5: warning: assignment
    discards 'const' qualifier from pointer target type
    [-Wdiscarded-qualifiers]

fixincl.c: extract_quoted_files() took the file name as const char *
but writes into it (it cuts the name at its last '/' to get the
directory).  Its only caller passes pz_curr_file, a char * buffer, so
the parameter is now char * (pz_file_name), the '/' search runs on that,
and pz_fixed_file stays a const char * so it can still point at "." when
the name has no directory.  Same writes, same output.

lto-plugin.c: process_symtab() and process_symtab_extension() only read
the suffix that strrchr finds (sscanf), so 's' becomes const char *.

No behaviour change.

